---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageIntro from '../components/PageIntro.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Design directions" description="A local comparison of the two visual directions considered for this website." currentPath="/design-directions/" noindex>
  <PageIntro number="A/B" eyebrow="Design study" title="Two directions" description="The same material, with a different center of gravity. The implemented site is a deliberate synthesis rather than a midpoint." />
  <div class="direction-grid">
    <section class="direction-sample direction-a">
      <p>Direction A / Academic Editorial</p>
      <h2>Rigorous, compact, bibliographic.</h2>
      <p>Smaller intervals, firmer rules, and metadata aligned for scanning.</p>
      <article class="sample-record"><span>20XX</span><div><h3>Untitled research record</h3><p>A clearly labeled layout sample—not a publication claim.</p></div></article>
    </section>
    <section class="direction-sample direction-b">
      <p>Direction B / Personal Editorial</p>
      <h2>Open, offset, quietly intimate.</h2>
      <p>More breathing room, stronger reading typography, and controlled asymmetry.</p>
      <article class="sample-record"><span>NOTE</span><div><h3>A deliberately long title showing how a personal text may occupy the page</h3><p>Writing is given its own rhythm without becoming a separate identity.</p></div></article>
    </section>
  </div>
  <div class="direction-notes">
    <p><strong>Recommendation:</strong> keep Direction A’s information architecture and bibliographic discipline, then borrow Direction B’s composition for the homepage and long-form reading. That synthesis is used throughout the working prototype.</p>
    <p lang="ja">長い日本語の見出しや本文でも、行間と余白が過度に詰まらないよう、和文には独立した組版設定を用意しています。</p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>

